# Default NonLinLoc control file used by the locnll SeisComP plugin (via
# screloc). LOCFILES/LOCSIG/LOCCOM are injected per-event by the plugin
# itself; this file supplies the fixed search/grid/model parameters.
#
# TRANS must exactly match what was used to build the DB1D travel-time
# grids (nonlinloc/run/vel2grid.in, grid2time.in) -- otherwise station and
# event positions would be projected inconsistently.
CONTROL 1 54321
TRANS SIMPLE 31.5 -104.0 0.0

LOCHYPOUT SAVE_NLLOC_ALL

LOCSEARCH OCT 10 10 4 0.01 20000 5000 0 1

# LOCGRID numx numy numz origx origy origz dx dy dz type save
# Must cover the whole scpyocto association area (pyocto.lat_min/max=28/35,
# pyocto.lon_min/max=-109/-99 in the live scpyocto.cfg) in the TRANS SIMPLE
# projection above, plus margin -- that's +-389km north-south and +-474km
# east-west from the (31.5,-104.0) origin. The previous +-150km box was far
# too small: events located near/outside the network edges landed on the
# grid boundary and got rejected outright ("max prob location on grid
# boundary N, rejecting location") or came back as an empty location,
# confirmed 2026-08-08 as the main reason the NonLinLoc relocation backlog
# wasn't draining. Widening this does not require regenerating the
# per-station travel-time tables (those are built radially per-station out
# to 300km via vel2grid.in/grid2time*.in, independent of this box), and
# NLLoc's OCT search cost is bounded by LOCSEARCH OCT's maxNumNodes/
# maxNumScatter below, not by this box's nominal size.
# Constrained 2026-08-19 to the network's actual association footprint.
# Previously 1101x941x66 from (-550,-470,-5), which spans lat 27.27-35.73,
# lon -109.80..-98.20 and depth -5..60 km -- materially LARGER than the region
# pyocto can even associate in (lat 28-35, lon -109..-99, depth 0-50). An
# unconverged inversion therefore ran to the grid walls and published a
# physically impossible hypocenter. Measured that day: 457 NLL origins landed
# outside the footprint, 42% of them sitting exactly on the old grid edge
# (lat 35.700/27.300 etc), and 209 events (2.17% since Aug 12) carried one as
# their PREFERRED origin. Ground-truth check against USGS on the 6 such events
# that had a ComCat match: NLL median error 524 km versus pyocto's 9 km on the
# same events -- i.e. relocation was destroying locations pyocto had right to
# within 0.6-0.9 km. Separately, z starting at -5.0 let 36.9% of ALL NLL origins
# be placed above sea level, which for ~1 km-elevation West Texas is impossible;
# z now starts at 0.0, matching pyocto's depth_min. Clipping to the footprint
# does not make an unconverged solution correct -- it will now pin at the
# footprint edge instead -- but it bounds the error at ~80 km rather than ~520 km
# and keeps every published hypocenter inside the region the network can sample.
LOCGRID  949 779 51  -474.0 -389.0 0.0  1.0 1.0 1.0  PROB_DENSITY SAVE

LOCMETH EDT_OT_WT 9999.0 4 -1 -1 -1 6 -1.0 1
LOCGAU 0.2 0.0
LOCGAU2 0.02 0.05 2.0
LOCPHASEID  P   P p Pn Pg
LOCPHASEID  S   S s Sn Sg
LOCQUAL2ERR 0.1 0.5 1.0 2.0 99999.9
LOCANGLES ANGLES_YES 5
LOCPHSTAT 9999.0 -1 9999.0 1.0 1.0 9999.9 -9999.9 9999.9
